WEBVTT

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.120
You did it, we're in second place.

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:18.510
But I lost the point race.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:24.610
It's up to you now.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:27.380
I'll do my best.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:46.190
Why is that girl wearing 
that weird glove?

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:46.190
East

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.880
Because her grandma 
runs a bowling alley.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:51.690
I saw that in some interview somewhere.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:53.120
You're back!

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:54.350
Good job.

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:57.710
So I guess it's like an 
advertisement for her business.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:00:58.950
That's so loyal.

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:01.720
It could be a charm or, like, 
a sort of battle cry.

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:03.030
It's so hot.

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.640
You got changed fast!

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:40.260
<b>Round 7: 
Conviction</b>

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.720
<i>I'll be fine.</i>

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:44.680
You keep asking the same thing.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.130
But if it runs long...

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:48.430
Then you might spend 
ten days over there.

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:50.930
I'm more worried about the alley.

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:52.380
Do you have enough help?

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:52.940
Yes.

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:56.690
Cousin Yukie-chan said she'll 
help on the weekend.

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:01.310
What about the weekdays? 
If you're all alone...

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:02.970
I'll be fine.

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:04.290
You just go do your best.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:06.040
It's okay, if you take first place.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:10.410
W-Win the nationals... that's...

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:12.850
I mean, you know.

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:15.390
You can go because 
you're with Harue-chan.

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:16.110
What?

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:18.870
What do you mean by that?

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:21.200
When Harue-chan went to the nationals,

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.820
you were watching the whole time.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:27.060
When she lost in the end, 
you cried like a baby.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:29.060
Why do you remember that?!

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:31.450
In the regional preliminaries,

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:33.460
you were having more fun 
than I've seen you have

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:36.900
playing mahjong in a long time.

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:41.580
I'll be watching the whole 
time I'm in the alley.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:45.660
Go get them! Go win that thing.

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:49.280
I'll do my best.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.430
Kentani High School (Hyougo)
1st Year - Fourth Player
Morigaki Yuuka

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:04.430
Hiya.

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:06.430
Koshigaya Girls' (Saitama)
3rd year - Fourth Player
Utsugi Tamago

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:06.430
Cheers!

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:08.430
Senriyama Girls' (North Osaka)
2nd year - Fourth Player
Funakubo Hiroko

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:08.430
Good luck.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:11.940
<i>We're still in the second round match.</i>

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:14.810
<i>We can't afford to lose here.</i>

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:17.810
Achiga Girls' (Nara)
2nd year - Fourth Player
Sagimori Arata

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.420
Good luck, everyone.

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:24.820
Do your best, Arata.

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:30.950
<i>We have to be cautious with the 
unknown first year from Kentani.</i>

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:32.660
<i>And...</i>

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:40.130
<i>And...</i>

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:40.070
<b>Ignore</b>

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:44.240
<i>All three of the upperclassmen</i>

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:46.090
<i>from Achiga are strange in some way,</i>

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:50.450
<i>but I haven't been able 
to analyze her...</i>

00:04:55.990 --> 00:04:57.980
The fourth players' match has begun!

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:04.860
This girl's kind of a mystery, huh?

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:08.260
Any oddity in her charts could 
just be statistical error.

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:11.350
Even if she has her weird habits, 
we've only got five games on her

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:13.600
between regional and nationals.

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:15.910
I guess it's stranger 
that we were able to see

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:18.250
the Matsumi sisters' habits 
with that little data.

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:22.430
She does have some quirks in her play style,

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:25.510
but we just don't have enough data.

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:28.750
I hope Hiroko will be okay.

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:30.140
What's wrong?

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:33.220
In a situation like this, 
she can't help

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:34.980
but analyze her opponents.

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:38.460
She's just a scientist, 
through and through.

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:43.540
I never imagined that I'd hand the match

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:45.900
over to our two 1st years in third place.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:48.330
As representative for the 
incompetent upperclassmen,

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:49.370
I'd like to apologize.

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:50.870
Oh, come on!

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:52.280
Kozue-chan!

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:54.520
You were up against 
Senriyama's Eguchi Sera!

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.120
It's not your fault.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:59.000
It's very possible for us to 
get back to second place.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:02.270
I'm sure Yuuka-chan will get us there.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.370
Tsumo!

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:22.190
2,000. 4,000.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:24.900
Wow, Yuuka-chan, you're fast.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:31.610
Ouch!

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:34.040
I can't sit like this.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:35.490
After only one hand?

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:41.180
Is this even going to work?

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:43.360
She used to live abroad, huh?

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:45.640
Do you think she can fit in with us?

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:48.340
I wonder if she's the 
one who has to fit in.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:53.480
It might actually be 
us who have to fit in.

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:55.010
What do you mean?

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:00.200
If we want to get better,

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:03.440
just following our traditions 
might not be enough.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:05.960
That's what I've been thinking...

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:11.680
Riichi!

00:07:14.170 --> 00:07:16.040
Three tiles from tenpai... 
Guess I'm giving up.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:17.040
Chi!

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:18.450
[Ippatsu - winning in the turn after declaring "riichi"]

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:18.450
No ippatsu for you!

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:30.970
Tsumo!

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:32.840
8,000 from all.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:33.830
Dealer Baiman.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:37.120
[Oya baiman = dealer baiman. Baiman = double 
mangan. Mangan = 8000 points; dealer gets 1.5x 
multiplier, so 8000 x 2 x 1.5 = 24,000 points]

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:35.100
Senriyama Girls' (North Osaka)
2nd year - Fourth Player
Funakubo Hiroko

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:37.100
Koshigaya Girls' (Saitama)
3rd year - Fourth Player
Utsugi Tamago

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:39.980
<i>We're in third place again.</i>

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:42.980
Achiga Girls' (Nara)
2nd year - Fourth Player
Sagimori Arata

00:07:41.570 --> 00:07:42.530
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:47.480
Kentani High School (Hyougo)
1st Year - Fourth Player
Morigaki Yuuka

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:44.920
Fresh out of the gate as dealer,

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:46.920
Kentani's Morigaki starts the first hand with 
a resounding Dealer Baiman Tsumo,

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:49.230
putting them right into second place!

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:51.080
Yuuka-chan's amazing!

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:52.770
Yeah. She really did it.

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:53.990
We might have a real shot now!

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:01.410
<i>I need to get this back.</i>

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:24.430
Tsumo!

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:27.480
1,300 - 2,600!

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:32.490
And the match between the 
fourth players is over!

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:35.110
Senriyama Girls' (North Osaka)
2nd year - Fourth Player
Funakubo Hiroko

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:35.930
Senriyama continues to 
lead by a wide margin,

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:40.120
Kentani High School (Hyougo)
1st Year - Fourth Player
Morigaki Yuuka

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:37.710
but Morigaki's great effort

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:39.480
has put Kentani in second place.

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:40.120
Yes!

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:40.520
Koshigaya Girls' (Saitama)
3rd year - Fourth Player
Utsugi Tamago

00:08:40.390 --> 00:08:43.900
Nooooooo!

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:47.190
The battle for second place will 
be between Kentani and Achiga

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:49.750
Koshigaya Girls' (Saitama)
3rd year - Fourth Player
Utsugi Tamago

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:49.750
as Koshigaya ended up falling 
behind quite a bit.

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:52.760
Achiga Girls' (Nara)
2nd year - Fourth Player
Sagimori Arata

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:54.710
<i>I couldn't reach them...</i>

00:08:57.670 --> 00:09:00.050
<i>The unexplainable discards she 
makes from time to time...</i>

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:01.550
<i>If I go back and analyze her discards,</i>

00:09:01.550 --> 00:09:03.590
<i>I wonder if I can figure 
out the reasoning behind it.</i>

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:09.980
<i>She's certainly quite an 
interesting specimen!</i>

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:17.490
You did well, Arata.

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:18.890
<b>Kentani</b>

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:23.120
Now it's your turn!

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:24.410
Yeah.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:28.520
<b>Achiga</b>

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:30.620
We will now proceed to 
the fifth players' match!

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:34.670
Here I go!

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:36.630
We're counting on you, Shizu!

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:39.370
I got this!

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:46.450
12,000!

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:49.650
Achiga Girls' Academy's 
Takakamo Shizuno has just

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:51.320
[Stealth Haneman - Not declaring riichi while 
in tenpai; haneman - 1.5 mangan]

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:51.320
dealt into a stealth haneman!

00:09:51.640 --> 00:09:52.690
That's really painful in the

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:54.740
third hand of the second half's south round.

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:56.740
<i>On the eighth turn, huh?</i>

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.520
<i>That was quite careless,</i>

00:09:58.520 --> 00:10:00.320
<i>even though it was her
 last time as the dealer.</i>

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:03.330
Achiga Girls' (Nara)
1st year - Fifth Player
Takakamo Shizuno

00:10:05.310 --> 00:10:08.340
It's finally the final hand of the match, 
the last hand of the second half

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:09.580
of the fifth players' match.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:17.350
<i>Ugh, this is bad, this is bad!</i>

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:19.430
<i>My hand sucks, too!</i>

00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:22.180
<i>But...</i>

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:26.180
Shizu...

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:30.560
East (Dealer)
Senriyama Girls' (North Osaka)
3rd year - Fifth Player
Shimizudani Ryuuka

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:33.570
South
Kentani High School (Hyougo)
1st Year - Fifth Player
Yasufuku Riko

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:36.570
West
Koshigaya Girls' (Saitama)
2nd year - Fifth Player
Yagihara Keiko

00:10:36.630 --> 00:10:39.280
North
Achiga Girls' (Nara)
1st year - Fifth Player
Takakamo Shizuno

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:45.700
<i>But...</i>

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:50.330
<i>that's still no reason to quit!</i>

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.250
The final hand has begun.

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:54.530
For dealer Senriyama,

00:10:54.530 --> 00:10:56.810
moving on to the semi-finals 
is essentially guaranteed,

00:10:56.810 --> 00:10:58.050
so they will end the match if they win

00:10:58.050 --> 00:10:59.580
the hand, or the hand is a draw.

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:01.220
Therefore, there won't be any renchan,

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:03.400
meaning this is the final hand.

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:06.310
In second place, Kentani 
has 93,600 points.

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:07.720
Behind them in third is Achiga Girls',

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:09.520
with 81,700 points.

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:12.270
To take second, Achiga would 
need more than a haneman tsumo,

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:14.900
or a direct hit on Kentani 
of more than 6,400 points.

00:11:15.290 --> 00:11:18.930
Who will take second place and move on?

00:11:18.930 --> 00:11:21.690
Or will the trailing Koshigaya Girls' show that

00:11:21.690 --> 00:11:22.780
they have fight left in them?

00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:28.040
<i>I got it!</i>

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:30.870
<i>A possible comeback hand, 
as high as a haneman!</i>

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:32.880
<i>But...</i>

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:36.680
<i>if I get the cheaper 4 of bamboos,</i>

00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:38.130
<i>I'd need to declare riichi</i>

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:39.560
<i>and get ura dora to make it.</i>

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:40.210
[Ura dora - reverse dora when calling riichi. 
Tiles under open dora indicators are flipped when 
they win to double the number of indicators.]

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:42.910
<i>If the hand is a draw, we're out.</i>

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:45.830
<i>I'm going to stay quiet and wait 
for that last 1 of bamboo.</i>

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:53.240
<i>It took her a while to discard 
that red 5 of circles.</i>

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:55.480
<i>She must be in tenpai.</i>

00:11:55.770 --> 00:11:57.340
<i>Even being hit with a yakuman</i>

00:11:57.340 --> 00:11:59.280
<i>won't change us being in first place.</i>

00:12:00.830 --> 00:12:02.740
<i>That was my cheap win tile!</i>

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:05.690
<i>I've got a bad feeling about this...</i>

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:08.740
<i>If I can hold on for just this hand,</i>

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:10.250
<i>we'll go to the semi-finals.</i>

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:20.880
<i>In the same turn?!</i>

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:24.710
Her last high winning tile

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:26.790
was discarded when she couldn't win with it.

00:12:26.790 --> 00:12:28.390
Now what are we going to do?

00:12:29.230 --> 00:12:32.230
Is this the end for us?

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:40.820
Not yet!

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:44.490
Shizu-chan won't give up.

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:48.230
We should all know that.

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:51.650
I think it's almost decided

00:12:51.650 --> 00:12:54.050
that it'll be Senriyama and Kentani.

00:12:54.050 --> 00:12:57.030
Should the announcer be making that call

00:12:57.030 --> 00:12:58.790
before the game is over?

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:00.550
Look at her face.

00:13:00.890 --> 00:13:03.880
If anything, I'd say 
something's just begun.

00:13:27.880 --> 00:13:29.160
[San Ankou - three closed triplets]

00:13:27.880 --> 00:13:29.160
A san ankou.

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:31.790
I was thinking in that direction,

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:35.880
but both 2 of bamboo and a 1 of 
characters are already discarded.

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:39.790
She has to draw the remaining 
1 of characters herself.

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:42.640
Ugh, speak of the devil!

00:13:45.190 --> 00:13:47.590
<i>So I can't go for a san 
ankou tsumo, either.</i>

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:13.310
A chiitoitsu...

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:13.310
[Chiitoitsu / chiitoi - seven pairs]

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:15.790
She has two dora, so a 
tsumo would be a mangan,

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:17.250
a hit would be 6,400!

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:19.120
But unless she hits Kentani directly,

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:20.210
it won't do any good.

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:26.550
<i>Not this one.</i>

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:29.320
<i>This girl...</i>

00:14:32.030 --> 00:14:33.720
<i>She hasn't given up yet.</i>

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:45.050
<i>This should be fine.</i>

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:48.450
<i>Ron!</i>

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:53.430
<i>6,400!</i>

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:56.370
[Yamagoshi Chiitoi - ignoring a winning tile, 
then instead winning off somebody after discarding]

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:56.370
<i>A yamagoshi chiitoi...</i>

00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:00.580
That's...

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:02.840
...a clean hit.

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:05.210
The match is over!

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:08.560
Originally in third place, Achiga Girls' 
Academy's Takakamo scored a direct

00:15:08.560 --> 00:15:10.970
hit for 6,400 on second place 
Kentani's Yasufuku!

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:12.560
A comeback in the very last hand!

00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:14.250
Achiga is now in second place!

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:15.720
The two schools going to 
the semi-finals are:

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:18.130
North Osaka's Senriyama Girls'

00:15:18.130 --> 00:15:21.000
and Nara's Achiga Girls' Academy!

00:15:22.180 --> 00:15:24.860
Yeah!

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:26.360
She did it!

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:29.990
She did it!

00:15:41.130 --> 00:15:43.080
<i>She played into a stealth haneman</i>

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:44.540
<i>right before and then did this...</i>

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:46.800
<i>This girl doesn't give up.</i>

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:49.080
<i>Not bad at all,</i>

00:15:52.860 --> 00:15:56.250
<i>but we won't be congratulating 
you guys anymore!</i>

00:15:57.330 --> 00:15:59.040
<b>Senriyama Girls'</b>

00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:00.310
It looks like we'll be playing

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:02.000
Achiga Girls' Academy again
 in the semi-finals.

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:05.120
You look pretty happy about that.

00:16:05.120 --> 00:16:07.190
You like the bowling girl that much?

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:12.950
Sh-She's just a specimen for my studies!

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:15.640
Well, we won't be able
 to pull any punches

00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:17.760
the next time we're 
up against those girls.

00:16:18.270 --> 00:16:19.580
True.

00:16:20.730 --> 00:16:21.990
I guess so.

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:26.030
The second round matches 
in Block A are finished,

00:16:26.030 --> 00:16:30.010
and unfortunately Hyougo prefecture's 
Kentani High School

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:31.930
and Saitama prefecture's Koshigaya Girls'

00:16:31.930 --> 00:16:34.060
did not qualify for the next round.

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:46.960
Cheers!

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:48.860
Congrats for getting in the top eight!

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:50.400
Congratulations!

00:16:50.680 --> 00:16:53.000
What a relief, huh, onee-chan?

00:16:56.190 --> 00:16:58.240
Man, that tastes so grown-up!

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:57.780
<b>So fast!</b>

00:16:58.560 --> 00:17:00.050
It's just barley tea.

00:17:00.050 --> 00:17:01.880
It's so good in the summer!

00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:04.670
If you don't keep your 
celebration in check,

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:06.530
the day after tomorrow will be rough.

00:17:07.350 --> 00:17:10.250
How big was Senriyama's lead today?

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:12.130
90,000 points...

00:17:12.660 --> 00:17:14.460
In the semi-final, 
the day after tomorrow,

00:17:14.460 --> 00:17:17.300
you'll be up against a school 
tougher than Senriyama.

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:22.680
Shiraitodai.

00:17:24.550 --> 00:17:26.430
Over here, please!

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:28.990
First off, we'd like to congratulate you

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:30.150
on advancing to the semi-finals.

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:32.530
We might be witnessing the first 
3-year consecutive champion.

00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:34.360
Can you comment on that?

00:17:36.090 --> 00:17:38.150
Hey, Teru.

00:17:41.090 --> 00:17:42.190
The biggest goal for us

00:17:42.190 --> 00:17:43.990
is to get our third 
consecutive championship!

00:17:44.550 --> 00:17:45.520
That is another reason

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:47.460
why we simply can't lose 
in the semi-finals.

00:17:47.970 --> 00:17:50.130
There are a lot of tough 
teams again this year,

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:51.590
so we're really looking 
forward to our matches.

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:54.080
We're going to do our best!

00:17:54.080 --> 00:17:56.090
Thank you for all your support!

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:07.600
Good work!

00:18:08.800 --> 00:18:12.320
Your business smile is as nasty as ever.

00:18:12.740 --> 00:18:16.540
But I truly am grateful to a 
lot of people in my heart.

00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:18.770
I didn't lie.

00:18:21.020 --> 00:18:24.460
What I mean is that you're just 
so different from normal.

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:29.390
I really think their third 
championship is happening.

00:18:29.390 --> 00:18:30.770
Looks like it.

00:18:30.770 --> 00:18:33.780
It could've been a good fight 
if Senriyama had Arakawa Kei

00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:36.010
and Atago Hiroe in their roster.

00:18:36.450 --> 00:18:40.260
As it is, Shiraitodai 
is the clear winner.

00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:45.270
That's right.

00:18:45.570 --> 00:18:49.000
Senriyama, the school that was 
90,000 points ahead of you;

00:18:49.660 --> 00:18:52.400
Shiraitodai, who is even 
stronger than them;

00:18:52.870 --> 00:18:55.680
and then the Fukuoka 
powerhouse, Shindouji.

00:18:55.680 --> 00:18:57.150
If you can't get second place

00:18:57.150 --> 00:18:59.800
among those three schools,
 you won't make it to the finals.

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:03.620
Ugh, we knew what we 
were up against, but...

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:05.310
The press thinks

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:09.410
our chances of getting to 
the finals are dismal at best.

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:11.080
Or less nicely put,

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:12.290
"out of the question."

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:21.960
I'll attend the coaches' meeting now

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:23.550
and then I'll eat dinner out.

00:19:23.800 --> 00:19:27.520
Order room service and 
just take it easy today.

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:35.320
Harue seemed to be kind of on edge.

00:19:35.710 --> 00:19:39.650
Of course. Next is that semi-final match.

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:41.700
Semi-finals...

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:46.890
The obstacle Haru-chan couldn't clear.

00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:49.020
Oh, yeah.

00:20:01.310 --> 00:20:04.180
I want to eat ramen! Ramen!

00:20:12.370 --> 00:20:14.370
So, why ramen, all of a sudden?

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:18.630
Well, it's not every day 
that you get a chance

00:20:18.630 --> 00:20:20.520
to eat Tokyo's famous ramen!

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:25.940
It's Akado-san!

00:20:26.900 --> 00:20:31.210
It's Harue and... who 
is that person again?

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:35.080
That's Kumakura-san. 
She was Fukuoka's coach.

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:39.340
Wow, your eyes are just too good.

00:20:40.430 --> 00:20:41.510
Here they come!

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:44.500
So, why are we hiding, anyway?

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:46.260
Because we got scolded before?

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:51.810
So what about going pro?

00:20:56.230 --> 00:20:59.230
Getting these girls to 
the semi-finals in the

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:01.490
nationals is a big plus for you.

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:05.930
I'll send you a proper email 
about all that later.

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:07.730
All right.

00:21:10.090 --> 00:21:14.260
You mean Harue was just using 
us for this, all along?

00:21:14.260 --> 00:21:16.330
No... well...

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:17.960
Of course not!

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:20.460
Haru-chan would never 
do something like that!

00:21:20.870 --> 00:21:23.290
But she said herself 
that there's no way

00:21:23.290 --> 00:21:25.390
we can win with 
such a huge score-gap.

00:21:25.390 --> 00:21:27.560
She's basically given up on us!

00:21:28.280 --> 00:21:32.850
This is all because 
I lost all those points.

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:34.350
No, that's not what...

00:21:36.340 --> 00:21:37.580
Sorry, onee-chan!

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:39.080
I'm over here.

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:40.440
Huh?

00:21:41.170 --> 00:21:42.940
Then whose pillows are these?

00:21:52.860 --> 00:21:55.360
She just appeared out of nowhere!

00:21:58.890 --> 00:22:00.540
What's up, Momo?

00:22:00.800 --> 00:22:03.940
I was in a hurry and I ran into someone.

00:22:03.940 --> 00:22:05.700
You need to watch out.

00:22:05.700 --> 00:22:07.590
I'm very sorry.

00:22:07.590 --> 00:22:11.180
No, I'm sorry. I'm the one who 
wasn't watching where I was going.

00:22:11.180 --> 00:22:15.810
Wait a second. 
Aren't you... Touyoko-san?

00:22:17.080 --> 00:22:18.520
How do you know my name?

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:20.180
Huh? Who?

00:22:20.180 --> 00:22:22.020
Don't you remember?

00:22:22.020 --> 00:22:24.280
They showed us the recordings 
of the Nagano matches!

00:22:26.650 --> 00:22:28.220
You're right!

00:22:28.220 --> 00:22:29.400
You're the girl who got more points

00:22:29.400 --> 00:22:31.380
in the fourth players' match than 
either Nodoka or Touka-san!

00:22:31.380 --> 00:22:32.370
Don't point!

00:22:32.660 --> 00:22:34.620
Are you friends with Boob-san?

00:22:35.170 --> 00:22:37.120
Touka-san told us about

00:22:37.660 --> 00:22:40.880
Tsuruga Academy's disappearing 1st year,

00:22:40.880 --> 00:22:42.990
Stealth Momo.

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:19.930
<b>Training</b>

00:24:05.910 --> 00:24:08.210
Shizu, how many of those 
jerseys do you have?

00:24:08.210 --> 00:24:11.390
Including sleeved and sleeveless, 
one, two, three...

00:24:11.390 --> 00:24:13.330
How about wearing something 
else for a change?

00:24:13.330 --> 00:24:14.930
I can lend you some of my clothes.

00:24:14.930 --> 00:24:16.180
No thanks.

00:24:16.180 --> 00:24:17.310
Why not?

00:24:17.310 --> 00:24:18.580
The size...

00:24:19.930 --> 00:24:26.000
<b>Please tune in again!</b>
